# Build context for deploy/backend.Dockerfile (the api, mcp, and store images).
#
# Why an allowlist: the repo root holds a real .env with live secrets, a
# local SQLite database with users' contracts, per-user Stripe Link logins in
# .handshake-state/, and the owner's _incoming/ copies. A denylist that
# forgets one new file ships it into an image (and to Fly's remote builder).
# So everything is excluded first and only what the Python images need is
# let back in. The frontend has its own context and ignore file
# (frontend/.dockerignore).

*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!handshake/
!merchant_static/
!deploy/backend.Dockerfile
!deploy/api-entrypoint.sh

# Re-exclude anything sensitive or generated that could sit inside the
# allowed folders (defense in depth: these must never reach an image even if
# someone drops one there).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/link-card*.json
**/.link-tmp
**/.handshake-state
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/*.egg-info
**/.DS_Store
